#: deployment/exporter.py:129
#, python-brace-format
msgid "NixBerry: offline ISO installation\n\n1. Verify sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.\n2. Create a new VM with UEFI, Secure Boot disabled and exactly one blank disk.\n   CPU, RAM, disk and network parameters are in manifest.json; the target disk must be {disk}.\n   Use the guest agent and controller for the platform described in recipe/README.md.\n3. Attach {filename} and boot the VM from it. The ISO already contains the system and disko.\n4. Transfer INSTALL-ISO.sh to the installation VM over SSH or another medium.\n   First verify the VM identity in the hypervisor console and its actual DMI UUID:\n   cat /sys/class/dmi/id/product_uuid\n5. Read-only check (replace UUID with the verified value):\n   bash INSTALL-ISO.sh dry-run UUID {system} {disko} {bytes} {profile} {disk}\n   After checking, repeat the same command with apply instead of dry-run.\n   Installation refuses disks with partitions or signatures; it does not reinstall an existing system.\n6. Shut down the VM gracefully, detach the ISO and boot from disk.\n   Verify networking and readlink -f /run/current-system against manifest.json.\n\nThe operator prepares the hypervisor network. System networking follows manifest.json.\n"
msgstr ""

